Requirements: 9   with obligations: 9

[task-01] The review can run a named set of a project's tests and observe what each one
    does, rather than only reading them. The run happens in an isolated sandbox. A test
    that reaches for the network does not reach it. No credential held by the machine
    that launched the run is visible to the code under test. The run is bounded by a
    time budget, and when that budget is exhausted the run stops cleanly, leaving
    nothing still executing behind it.
    -> observe-test-behavior  [functional/explicit]
       The review can run a named set of a project's tests and observe what each one
       does, rather than only reading them.
    -> isolated-sandbox  [invariant/explicit]
       The run happens in an isolated sandbox.
    -> network-access-blocked-for-tests  [functional/explicit]
       A test that reaches for the network is prevented from reaching it.
    -> no-launch-credentials-visible  [invariant/explicit]
       No credential held by the machine that launched the run is visible to the code
       under test.
    -> clean-timeout-stop  [functional/explicit]
       The run stops cleanly when the time budget is exhausted.

[task-02] Every test the run was asked about ends with a recorded outcome: it completed
    and passed, it completed and failed, it was blocked reaching the network, it
    exhausted its time, or it was never started. An outcome that is not a completed run
    carries the reason it is not, so that a test the runner tried and could not complete
    stays distinguishable from one it never tried.
    -> test-outcome-recorded  [invariant/explicit]
       Every test the run was asked about ends with a recorded outcome.
    -> noncompleted-outcome-carries-reason  [invariant/explicit]
       Every outcome that is not a completed run carries the reason it is not.
    -> distinguish-tried-from-never-started  [invariant/explicit]
       A test the runner tried and could not complete stays distinguishable from one it
       never tried.

[task-03] A run that does not complete leaves the review's conclusions where they were.
    Evidence with no completed run behind it stays at the static tier, and that is an
    ordinary result rather than a failure.
    -> run-incomplete-leaves-conclusions-unchanged  [invariant/explicit]
       A run that does not complete leaves the review's conclusions where they were.
    -> evidence-without-completed-run-stays-static-tier  [invariant/explicit]
       Evidence with no completed run behind it stays at the static tier.
    -> ordinary-result-not-failure  [invariant/explicit]
       Treat the static-tier result for evidence with no completed run behind it as an
       ordinary result rather than a failure.
    -> ordinary-result-not-failure-2  [invariant/explicit]
       Treat this as an ordinary result rather than a failure.

[constraint-01] Only the named tests are run. There is no path through which the whole
    suite runs.
    -> only-named-tests-run  [functional/explicit]
       Only the named tests are run; the review does not execute the project's full
       suite through any alternate path.

[constraint-02] A time budget applies both to a single test and to the run as a whole.
    -> single-test-time-budget  [boundary/explicit]
       A single test is subject to a time budget.
    -> run-wide-time-budget  [boundary/explicit]
       The run as a whole is subject to a time budget.

[constraint-03] The time budgets and the interpreter the tests run under are
    configuration with conservative defaults, and neither is read from the project under
    review.
    -> time-budget-and-interpreter-defaults  [docs_config/explicit]
       The time budgets and the interpreter the tests run under use conservative
       configuration defaults, and neither setting is read from the project under
       review.

[exclusion-01] Choosing which tests to run, and deciding whether a project's tests can
    be run at all.
    -> do-not-decide-test-selection-or-runnability  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter choosing which tests to run or deciding whether a
       project's tests can be run at all.

[exclusion-02] Altering the code under test in order to observe what a test does.
    -> no-code-alteration-for-observation  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter the code under test in order to observe what a test
       does.

[exclusion-03] Recording which lines a test executed.
    -> no-line-execution-recording  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not record which lines a test executed.

